                <pb facs="0512" n="500" sameAs="frus:frus1939v01/pg500"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 European War 1939/17: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Rumania</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gunther</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-10-03T19:00:00-05:00">October 3, 1939—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>165. Your 296, October 2, 5 p.m. No indications have been received here as to any
                    desire on the part of the belligerents for a peace initiative to be taken from
                    here and of course no steps are under contemplation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
